[College: Accounting] Gross AR and bad debts?
I posted this to r/Accounting but no one responded.

&amp;#x200B;

I'm trying to find the net and gross accounts receivable (AR) and bad debt expense from real life sample statements. Net AR is easy. It has its own line on the balance sheet.

&amp;#x200B;

What is throwing me off is that there is a non current AR line in the long-term assets. This of course adds to the total assets, but I don't know if it applies to gross accounts receivable. In past homework, there hasn't been a line like this presented. The only way to calculate gross AR that I know is to add net AR and the Allowance for doubtful accounts. There is no line for allowance; it is off in a paragraph several pages down. I'm probably overthinking it, but googling hasn't answered my questions and so I wanted to be more certain.

&amp;#x200B;

There is also no line for bad debt expense or anything sounding like that on the income statement, balance sheet, or cash flow statement. I'm supposed to compare and see if their bad debt expense was higher/lower than their write off for AR, but I don't know how I'm supposed to find that if the expense is not provided.
